---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import {defaults,limits} from '../../../../../public/equipment/16-07/solver.mjs';
const base='/equipment/16-07/', sheet='https://www.fishersci.de/content/dam/fssite/eu/brands/f/22640_fisherbrand/11475_Fisherbrand_Isotemp_water_baths_EN.pdf', photos='https://shop.unigreenscheme.co.uk/general-laboratory/water-baths-and-chillers/water-baths/fisher-scientific-isotemp-gpd-05-water-bath';
const labels={setC:'Bath set point (°C)',bath0C:'Initial bath (°C)',dummy0C:'Initial dummy (°C)',tauBathS:'Bath time constant (s)',tauDummyS:'Dummy time constant (s)',durationS:'Exposure duration (s)'};
---
<Layout pageTitle="Isotemp GPD 05 · inert heat transfer" description="Watch a synthetic inert mass approach a controlled bath temperature and verify the one-time-constant rule." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment wb"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-07/">← Equipment 16-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#wb-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">16-07 · BENCH HEAT TRANSFER / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Fisher Isotemp GPD 05</h2><p>Run a hypothetical thermal dummy in a held-temperature bath. At one time constant the model closes about 63.2% of the initial temperature gap.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>5 L bench bath</h3><div id="wb-view" aria-label="Orbitable metric GPD 05 with hinged clear lid, stainless interior, tray, dummy, probe and digital display"></div><div class="bar"><button data-wb-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-wb-view="tank">Tank close-up</button><button data-wb-view="rear">Rear</button><button id="wb-lid">Open lid</button></div><p id="wb-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit; pinch or scroll to zoom. Click the black handle to lift the transparent lid and inspect the stainless chamber.</p></section>
<section><h3>Synthetic thermal dummy</h3><div class="fields"><label>Bath model<select id="wb-mode"><option value="held">Held at set point</option><option value="relaxing">Relax toward set point</option></select></label>
{Object.entries(labels).map(([key,label])=><label>{label}<input type="number" id={'wb-'+key} min={limits[key][0]} max={limits[key][1]} step="any" value={defaults[key]}/></label>)}</div><div class="bar"><button id="wb-run" class="primary">Run thermal dummy</button><button id="wb-load">Remove inert dummy</button><button id="wb-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="wb-status" aria-live="polite">Inert dummy loaded; lid closed. Run the default example or edit the inputs.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Temperature history</h3><div class="grid"><canvas id="wb-chart" width="700" height="292" aria-label="Bath and inert dummy temperatures in degrees Celsius over simulated exposure time"/><div><output id="wb-results">No simulated exposure yet.</output><label>Scrub simulated time<input type="range" id="wb-seek" min="0" max="120" step="1" value="0" disabled/></label><div class="bar"><button id="wb-tau" disabled>Jump to one dummy time constant</button><button id="wb-json" disabled>History JSON</button><button id="wb-csv" disabled>History CSV</button></div></div></div></section>
<section id="wb-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: Fisher Isotemp GPD 05, 5 L, catalog 15375877, standard clear gable cover and diffuser tray; no optional rack. Dimensions are anchored to the <a href={sheet+'#page=2'}>Fisher brochure p. 2</a>. The <a href={sheet+'#page=1'}>brochure cover</a> shows family control and lid details, not this exact SKU. <a href={photos}>Photographs of a labeled GPD 05 from another catalog region</a> establish front, open lid, chamber and rear appearance; they do not establish dimensions for 15375877.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="640" height="435" src={base+'open.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original open-lid rendering of the stainless bath, gray control pod and inert dummy"/><figcaption>Original open view, not a photograph. Compared to photographed GPD 05 for lid hinge and visible tank; the bath probe and dummy are teaching geometry.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="640" height="435" src={base+'rear.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original rear rendering of hinge, lower connectors and ventilation"/><figcaption>Original rear view. Connector, hinge and vent spacing are undimensioned approximations.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification / test</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Without cover; working area</td><td>246 D × 355 W × 232 H mm; 154 D × 300 W × 150 H mm</td><td>Nominal body and tank geometry from Fisher p. 2. Lid, ports and rack details inferred.</td></tr><tr><td>Hardware context</td><td>5 L; ambient to 100 °C; ±0.1 °C stability and ±0.2 °C uniformity at 70 °C, p. 2</td><td>Not a simulator calibration or a suggested operating point. Set point inputs limited to 15–45 °C for the abstract exercise.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Held-bath one-τ case</td><td>28 °C bath, 18 °C dummy, τ = 60 s; 24.3212055883 °C at t = 60 s</td><td>24.3212055883 °C; 63.21205588% of initial gap; 10⁻¹⁰ °C analytical tolerance.</td></tr><tr><td>Relaxing bath, equal time constants</td><td>28 °C target, 21 °C initial bath, 18 °C initial dummy; both τ = 60 s</td><td>At 60 s, bath 25.42484391 °C and dummy 21.74604950 °C. See locked references.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The held bath is constant by definition. The inert dummy is a single uniform temperature obeying <code>dTdummy/dt=(Tbath−Tdummy)/τdummy</code>. In relaxing mode, <code>Tbath=Tset+(Tbath,0−Tset)exp(−t/τbath)</code> drives that equation. The code evaluates the exact convolution, including the equal-τ limit, and timestamps all outputs on a simulated clock. Lid and dummy interlocks control whether a run starts. The lid has no modeled effect on heat loss. No convection field, heater control, evaporation, specimen treatment, real thermal calibration, or actual bath performance is modeled.</p>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'isotemp-gpd05.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Locked reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-history.json'}>Output format example</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No downstream or headset validation claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-07/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.wb{max-width:76rem}.wb .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.wb section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.wb .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.43rem;margin:.58rem 0}.wb .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.52rem}.wb label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.18em;font-size:.91rem}.wb button,.wb input,.wb select{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.wb button{cursor:pointer}.wb button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.wb .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.wb #wb-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.wb #wb-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.wb #wb-chart,.wb img{width:100%;height:auto}.wb #wb-results{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.5rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.wb #wb-status.error{color:#a54a34}.wb .scroll{overflow:auto}.wb table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.wb td,.wb th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.wb figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.wb .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
